Bug: header static's prototype and definition get different link names

setStaticFunctionLinkName (src/semact.c) names a static after the file it is in
only for UsageDefined. The prototype is UsageDeclared and is named after
parsingConfig.fileName, the compilation unit, so it becomes main.c!helper while
the definition and the call are helper.h!helper. Renaming helper from main.c
would leave the prototype in helper.h unchanged.

The //& lines in that function are a pre-2016 symbol-table lookup that would have
reused the prototype's link name; it no longer compiles. The obvious fix is to
name every usage after p->position.file, but the exactPositionResolve branch
deliberately uses the compilation unit, so decide what that setting should mean
first. Follows on from the project-relative link name fix (b3d5949d).
